    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 222\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 5670-A, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the state finance law, in relation to the sharing\n      of revenue from gaming devices located within the county of  Madi-\n      son\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  In  2013,  a settlement agreement was reached between the State of New\nYork, the Oneida Nation, Madison  County,  and  Oneida  County  settling\nyears  of  litigation over property tax, land and reservation issues. As\npart of that agreement, the Oneida Nation makes a  \"Nation  Payment\"  to\nthe State of a certain percentage of revenues from its casinos.\n\n  This  bill would amend the State Finance Law and obligate the State to\npay Madison County an additional 25% of the Nation Payment  attributable\nto  gaming  devices in Madison County. This payment would be in addition\nto an annual $3.5 million payment that Madison County  already  receives\npursuant  to  the  2013  agreement,  as well as the one-time $11 million\npayment that Madison County received when it signed the agreement.\n\n  As drafted, this bill could compromise the  multi-party  compact  that\nhas  been  in  place since 2013. I am therefore constrained to veto this\nbill.\n\n  However, I recognize that Madison County is impacted by gaming devices\nlocated within its borders. Therefore, I am instructing the director  of\nthe Division of the Budget to communicate with the sponsors of this bill\nto review and explore a revenue sharing formula that would provide Madi-\nson  County  with  an  appropriate portion of the revenue generated from\nsuch gaming devices.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 222,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2016
   }
